<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Podgorica Assembly</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">November <a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/podgorica">Podgorica</a> Assembly was a gathering of elected representatives that met in Podgorica in November 1918, at the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. On 26 November it deposed King Nicholas I and the Petrović-Njegoš dynasty of Montenegro and voted for unconditional union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, soon part of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a>. Opponents considered it illegitimate, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christmas-uprising">Christmas Uprising</a> followed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/podgorica-assembly.jpg" alt="Podgorica Assembly" width="320" height="519" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Serbia1918.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
